---
// Merchant-facing DPA (OS-339). Source-of-truth content is mirrored in
// docs/compliance/dpa-template.md — keep the two in sync. The SCC annex and
// governing-law/liability terms are a placeholder pending legal review
// before launch, same as /terms.
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'September 13, 2026';
---

<Layout
	title="Data Processing Agreement — OrderSail"
	description="OrderSail's Data Processing Agreement for merchants who need one for their own compliance obligations."
>
	<section class="head">
		<p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
		<h1>Data Processing Agreement</h1>
		<p class="lede">Last updated {lastUpdated}.</p>
	</section>

	<article class="legal">
		<p>
			This Data Processing Agreement ("DPA") forms part of the <a
				href="/terms">Terms of Service</a
			> between OrderSail ("Processor," "we") and the merchant using OrderSail
			("Controller," "you," "Merchant"). It applies where OrderSail processes
			personal data on your behalf as described in our <a href="/privacy"
				>Privacy Policy</a
			>.
		</p>

		<h2 id="subject-matter">Subject matter & duration</h2>
		<p>
			OrderSail processes personal data as necessary to provide the Service —
			hosting your storefront and dashboard, processing orders and payments,
			arranging shipping, sending transactional email, and providing support —
			for the duration of your account, plus any period required afterward for
			legal, accounting, or fraud-prevention purposes.
		</p>

		<h2 id="processing-details">Nature, purpose & categories of processing</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>Data subjects:</strong> your customers (buyers) and staff.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Personal data:</strong> name, email, shipping address, order
				contents, and payment-transaction records. Cardholder data goes
				directly to Stripe — OrderSail never receives it.
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h2 id="processor-obligations">Processor obligations</h2>
		<p>OrderSail will:</p>
		<ol>
			<li>
				Process personal data only on your documented instructions (including
				via your use of the dashboard and API), unless required otherwise by
				law.
			</li>
			<li>Ensure personnel who process personal data are bound by confidentiality.</li>
			<li>Apply appropriate technical and organizational security measures.</li>
			<li>
				Not engage a new subprocessor without prior notice through the
				subprocessor list's change-notification mechanism, giving you an
				opportunity to object.
			</li>
			<li>
				Assist you, to the extent reasonably possible, with data subject
				rights requests, breach notification, and data-protection-impact
				assessments.
			</li>
			<li>Notify you without undue delay after becoming aware of a personal data breach affecting your data.</li>
			<li>
				At your choice, delete or return all personal data at the end of our
				engagement, except where retention is required by law.
			</li>
			<li>Make available information reasonably necessary to demonstrate compliance with this DPA.</li>
		</ol>

		<h2 id="subprocessors">Subprocessors</h2>
		<p>
			Current subprocessors: Stripe (payments), Shippo (shipping labels and
			rates), and Amazon Web Services (hosting and transactional email via
			SES). We'll notify you in advance of any new subprocessor, with an
			opportunity to object on reasonable data-protection grounds before it
			takes effect.
		</p>

		<h2 id="international-transfers">International transfers</h2>
		<p>
			Where personal data is transferred outside a jurisdiction your law
			recognizes as offering adequate protection, the transfer is governed by
			the Standard Contractual Clauses, incorporated by reference.
		</p>
		<p>
			<em
				>[Placeholder — the SCC module/annex text and governing-law/liability
				terms are pending legal review before launch.]</em
			>
		</p>

		<h2 id="execution">How this DPA takes effect</h2>
		<p>
			Using OrderSail as a data processor under applicable data protection law
			constitutes acceptance of this DPA. If you need a signed copy for your
			own records or a vendor-review process, email <a
				href="mailto:legal@ordersail.com">legal@ordersail.com</a
			>.
		</p>
	</article>
</Layout>

<style>
	.head {
		padding: 40px 0 32px;
	}
	.head h1 {
		font-family: Georgia, serif;
		font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
		line-height: 1.1;
		font-weight: 400;
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
		margin: 0 0 14px;
	}
	.lede {
		font-family: ui-monospace, monospace;
		font-size: 0.86rem;
		color: var(--ink-dim);
		margin: 0;
	}

	.legal {
		max-width: 68ch;
		padding-bottom: 90px;
		font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
		font-size: 0.98rem;
		line-height: 1.7;
		color: var(--ink);
	}
	.legal h2 {
		font-family: Georgia, serif;
		font-size: 1.3rem;
		font-weight: 400;
		margin: 40px 0 12px;
	}
	.legal p {
		margin: 0 0 16px;
	}
	.legal ul,
	.legal ol {
		margin: 0 0 16px;
		padding-left: 1.2em;
	}
	.legal li {
		margin: 0 0 8px;
	}
	.legal a {
		text-decoration: underline;
		text-underline-offset: 2px;
	}
</style>
